---
import Presentation from "../../../../components/Presentation.astro";
import Divider from "../../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
import { Code as CodeSnippet } from "astro:components";

//#region CodeSnippets
const Assign = `count ← count + 1
IF(count = 10)
{
  DISPLAY(count)
}`;

const Loops = `REPEAT 5 TIMES
{
  <block>
}

REPEAT UNTIL(x ≥ 10)
{
  <block>
}`;

const ListNotation = `scores ← [12, 8, 21]
DISPLAY(scores[1])
DISPLAY(LENGTH(scores))
copy ← scores`;

const Procedure = `PROCEDURE area(w, h)
{
  RETURN(w * h)
}

kitchen ← area(3, 4)`;

const Trace1 = `total ← 0
i ← 1
REPEAT UNTIL(i > 4)
{
  total ← total + i
  i ← i + 1
}
DISPLAY(total)`;

const Trace2 = `local w = 12
local steps = 0

while w > 0 do
    w = w - 5
    steps = steps + 1
end

print(steps)`;

const Trace3 = `local a = {1, 2, 3}
local b = a
b[1] = 99
print(a[1])`;
//#endregion
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a href="/courses/ap-csp-lua/" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3">
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Activity 1.26: Quarter 1 Exam</h1>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <Presentation>
            <section>
              <h2>Activity 1.26</h2>
              <h3 class="text-sn-theme">Quarter 1 Exam</h3>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Today</h2>
              <p>
                <b class="text-sn-theme">The documentation sheet is due at the
                door.</b> On paper. You will not have a computer this period.
              </p>
              <p>Then the exam. It takes the whole session.</p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Shape of It</h2>
              <div class="text-start">
                <dl>
                  <dt>Section I &mdash; 22 multiple choice</dt>
                  <dd>44 points, 36 minutes. That is about 1:38 each, which is exam pace.</dd>
                  <dt>Section II &mdash; three written</dt>
                  <dd>26 points, 19 minutes. Trace a loop, find an error, describe an algorithm.</dd>
                </dl>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sn-theme">
                70 points. The largest single thing in the quarter.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Reference Sheet Is on Your Desk</h2>
              <p>
                Same as May. <b class="text-sn-theme">Nothing on it needs
                memorizing</b> &mdash; but you have to be able to find things on
                it quickly.
              </p>
              <p class="text-body-secondary">
                Everything else is closed. No notes, no code, no computer.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>It Switches Notation Without Warning</h2>
              <p>
                Some questions are Lua. Some are exam notation.{" "}
                <b class="text-sn-theme">Nothing tells you which is coming.</b>
              </p>
              <p class="text-body-secondary">
                That is deliberate, and it is the only honest rehearsal for
                meeting exam notation cold in May.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Assignment and Comparison</h2>
              <Code code={Assign} frame="code" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p>
                <code>&larr;</code> stores. <code>=</code> asks.{" "}
                <b class="text-sn-theme">Lua writes those as <code>=</code> and{" "}
                <code>==</code></b>, which is the reverse trap.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Two Loops</h2>
              <Code code={Loops} frame="code" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p>
                <b class="text-sn-theme"><code>REPEAT UNTIL</code> is the
                inverse of <code>while</code></b> &mdash; it repeats until the
                condition becomes true.
              </p>
              <p class="text-body-secondary">
                And <code>REPEAT n TIMES</code> gives you no counter. If you
                need one, you make it.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Lists</h2>
              <Code code={ListNotation} frame="code" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p>
                First element is <code>[1]</code> in both.{" "}
                <b class="text-sn-theme">But <code>copy &larr; scores</code>{" "}
                copies, and Lua's version does not.</b>
              </p>
              <p class="text-body-secondary">
                An out-of-range index terminates the program on the exam. In Lua
                it hands back <code>nil</code> and waits.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Procedures</h2>
              <Code code={Procedure} frame="code" lang="txt" showLineNumbers={false} />
              <p>
                <code>PROCEDURE</code> for both kinds.{" "}
                <code>RETURN</code> takes parentheses.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>The Three That Catch People</h2>
              <ul>
                <li>A typed value is a <b>string</b> until <code>tonumber</code></li>
                <li>Assigning a table makes an <b>alias</b> in Lua and a <b>copy</b> on the exam</li>
                <li><code>love.draw</code> is <b>not</b> a student-developed procedure</li>
              </ul>
              <p class="text-body-secondary">
                Sessions 4, 19 and 23. All three are on the paper.
              </p>
            </section>

            <section>
              <h2>Good Luck</h2>
              <p>
                Twenty-five sessions ago you ran a program that printed one
                line.
              </p>
              <p class="text-sn-theme">
                Read every question twice. Answer the easy ones first.
              </p>
            </section>
          </Presentation>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Prepare -->
        <section id="prepare">
          <h2>How to Prepare</h2>

          <p>
            <b class="text-sn-theme">This page is your revision, and it is
            homework the night before</b> &mdash; along with the documentation
            sheet.
          </p>

          <h3 class="mt-4">Work Through the Section Summaries</h3>

          <p>
            One per part of the quarter. Each one has the ideas, the traps, and
            the exam notation for its sessions:
          </p>

          <ul>
            <li><a href="./sum-getting-started">Getting Started</a> &mdash; sessions 1&ndash;6</li>
            <li><a href="./sum-motion-and-decisions">Motion and Decisions</a> &mdash; sessions 7&ndash;14</li>
            <li><a href="./sum-loops-and-tables">Loops and Tables</a> &mdash; sessions 15&ndash;20</li>
            <li><a href="./sum-functions">Functions</a> &mdash; sessions 21&ndash;23</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="mt-4">Three Traces, Right Now</h3>

          <p>
            Do these on paper before you read any further. Write the answer
            down, then check it.
          </p>

          <p><b>1.</b> What does this display?</p>

          <Code code={Trace1} lang="txt" frame="code" title="Exam notation" showLineNumbers={false} />

          <p><b>2.</b> What does this print?</p>

          <Code code={Trace2} lang="lua" frame="code" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} />

          <p><b>3.</b> What does this print?</p>

          <Code code={Trace3} lang="lua" frame="code" title="Lua" showLineNumbers={false} />

          <div class="alert alert-info">
            <b>Answers: 10, 3, and 99.</b> If you got the third one wrong, read{" "}
            <a href="./1-19">Activity 1.19</a> again &mdash; it is the sharpest
            difference between Lua and the exam and it is on the paper.
          </div>

          <h3 class="mt-4">The Checklist</h3>

          <p>Everything below is fair game. Tick what you can do without looking:</p>

          <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <ul>
                <li>Read <code>&larr;</code> and <code>=</code> correctly</li>
                <li>Translate a Lua comparison into exam notation</li>
                <li>Say what <code>MOD</code> gives you</li>
                <li>Say what <code>/</code> does <b>not</b> do</li>
                <li>Explain why a typed value is a string</li>
                <li>Trace an <code>if</code> / <code>elseif</code> chain</li>
                <li>Combine conditions with <code>and</code>, <code>or</code>, <code>not</code></li>
              </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
              <ul>
                <li>Count the passes of a <code>while</code> loop</li>
                <li>Count the passes of a <code>REPEAT UNTIL</code></li>
                <li>Say what a nested loop does</li>
                <li>Index a table from 1</li>
                <li>Say what <code>#t</code> gives you</li>
                <li>Say what a function with no <code>return</code> gives back</li>
                <li>Say which procedures the Create Task counts</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h3 class="mt-4">On the Day</h3>

          <ul>
            <li>
              <b class="text-sn-theme">Documentation sheet in your hand at the
              door.</b> Not on a computer
            </li>
            <li>Bring something to write with, and something to write with when that runs out</li>
            <li>The reference sheet is provided. Nothing else</li>
            <li>36 minutes on Section I, then move &mdash; the written section is 26 points</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Hand in the documentation sheet at the start of the period. The exam
            is collected at the end.
          </p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Quarter Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
